# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so anything not listed here is baked into
# an image layer and recoverable with `docker save` or a plain `docker run`.
# Gitignoring a file does nothing about that - see docs/SECURITY.md #23.

# Secrets. Supplied at runtime instead: env vars via docker-compose `env_file`,
# and the Firebase key via the read-only bind mount.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
firebase-service-account.json
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.p12
*.p8

# Build noise and one-off scripts that have no business in a release image.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
scratch/
scratch_db.py

.git
.gitignore
